  "notes": "University Park. Major code 'EARTHSCI' avoids colliding with the EARTH department prefix. This major requires 18 credits from ONE of five interdisciplinary minors (Climatology, Marine Science, Watersheds and Water Resources, Earth Systems, or Global Business Strategies) — assumed Earth Systems as the most directly related minor, modeled generically as 'Minor Course' slots since no live bulletin page names Earth Systems' own specific course list (only a differently-named 'Earth and Sustainability' minor currently has a standalone page, and it isn't confirmed to be the same minor). 'Supporting Course' pool (8-9 credits, bulletin: 'other approved courses') is also modeled generically. UPDATE after the prereq-parser fix: CHEM 110's real prereq is MATH 22, which was never in this plan -- and MATH 22 itself real-chains through MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3, none of which were present either, leaving CHEM 110 (and CHEM 111/112/113 after it) permanently unschedulable. Added MATH 3/MATH 4 (Semester 1) and MATH 21/MATH 22 (Semester 2) explicitly to complete the real chain, same fix and same convention as CHEM-2026.json's own build. Handbook-verification pass (2026-08-26): the live bulletin actually names exact course lists for the 'Introductory Earth Science' (15 credits) and 'Advanced Earth Science' (15 credits) categories, previously modeled as bare unfillable placeholders ('Intro GEOSC/EARTH elective' / 'Advanced EARTH elective') -- wired via a match regex on each slot so a real course from these lists is recognized. Dropped GEOG 110, GEOG 111, GEOG 412 (bare, non-W) and METEO 471 from the bulletin's own lists -- none exist in this app's scraped catalogs (GEOG 412W does exist and is used instead, matching the writing-intensive variant of that course). The bulletin's separate 3-credit 'Writing-Intensive' sub-requirement (one specific course from GEOG 310/412W, GEOSC 402Y/470W, or the now-uncataloged METEO 471) is not separately enforced -- the engine has no mechanism to require a specific one of several already-eligible electives be W-designated; deferred, same category as the grade-minimum tracking already deferred for other majors.",
